  <tag code="11.5" vocabulary="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">11.5 - By 2030, significantly reduce the number of deaths and the number of people affected and substantially decrease the direct economic losses relative to global gross domestic product caused by disasters, including water-related disasters, with a focus on protecting the poor and people in vulnerable situations</narrative>
  </tag>
  <tag code="13.1" vocabulary="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">13.1 - Strengthen resilience and adaptive capacity to climate-related hazards and natural disasters in all countries</narrative>
  </tag>
  <tag code="13.2" vocabulary="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">13.2 - Integrate climate change measures into national policies, strategies and planning</narrative>
  </tag>
  <tag code="13.3" vocabulary="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">13.3 - Improve education, awareness-raising and human and institutional capacity on climate change mitigation, adaptation, impact reduction and early warning</narrative>
  </tag>
  <tag code="13.B" vocabulary="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">13.b - Promote mechanisms for raising capacity for effective climate change-related planning and management in least developed countries and small island developing States, including focusing on women, youth and local and marginalized communities</narrative>
  </tag>
